    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d463">

                <pb facs="0452" n="440" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg440"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.51A/12–1544: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Tehran</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-15T14:00:00+03:25">December 15,
                            1944—2 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 2:08 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>932. The Prime Minister yesterday presented to the Medjliss a bill to repeal the
                    economic powers granted Millspaugh by the law of 13 <pb facs="0453" n="441"
                        xml:id="pg441"/> Ordibehesht, 1322<anchor n="45a" xml:id="d463-f1"/> and to
                    vest those same powers in the Cabinet which would be empowered to dissolve,
                    retain or transfer to other Ministries the economic organizations set up in the
                    Ministry of Finance under that law. The bill was referred to committee under
                    procedure of single urgency.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
